<Base title="Changelog | Tessera" description="What has changed in Tessera.">
  <Prose title="Changelog" intro="What is new in each version of Tessera.">
    <h2 id="1.0.2">1.0.2, 28 November 2026</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Smart Scan, Duplicates, Cleanup and Apps keep working, and keep their results, while you use other pages. A dot in the sidebar shows a page that is still working.</li>
      <li>Finding duplicates is much faster. Several files are compared at once, and the screen shows a progress bar, the time left and how much has been found so far.</li>
      <li>Cleanup shows steady progress on large folders and names the item it is working on, and Stop takes effect sooner.</li>
      <li>Delete permanently is much faster, on both Windows and Mac.</li>
      <li>Checkout asks only for your country and postcode.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="1.0.1">1.0.1, 27 November 2026</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Tessera for Mac, for Apple silicon and Intel Macs with macOS 12 or later, with the same features as on Windows.</li>
      <li>Cleanup now checks each item against the Recycle Bin’s size limit before moving it. An item too large for the Recycle Bin stays in place, with an explanation and the option to delete it permanently instead.</li>
      <li>Fixed: notices, such as an available update, could take up too much of the window.</li>
      <li>Tessera no longer offers to start when you sign in. Open it whenever you want to look at your storage.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="1.0.0">1.0.0, 27 November 2026</h2>
    <p>The first public release, for Windows 11 (64-bit).</p>
    <h3>Free</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Fast scans of any drive or folder, with results while it reads, and an interactive storage map of every folder to scale.</li>
      <li>Largest files, search with filters (name, type, size, date, empty folders), and highlighting on the map.</li>
      <li>Smart Scan suggestions that explain why each item was found and how safe it is to remove.</li>
      <li>An exact duplicate finder that compares file contents.</li>
      <li>Installed apps and their sizes, and a Restore page to put back anything Tessera moved.</li>
      <li>Scan a folder from its right-click menu in File Explorer (Show more options), or drop it on the window.</li>
      <li>Light, dark and high-contrast themes; keyboard navigation throughout.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Tessera Pro (one-time purchase)</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>A cleanup list for everything you choose: select all, filter and sort, then move to the Recycle Bin in one step, with progress, Stop and Undo.</li>
      <li>Plain answers when something can’t be removed, such as which app has a file open, with Try again. When an app holds a few files open inside a folder, Tessera can remove everything else.</li>
      <li>Delete permanently as a separate choice with its own warning.</li>
      <li>Free up space from OneDrive files while keeping them in the cloud, uninstall apps, storage history, CSV and printable reports.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Scans stay on your computer. Tessera goes online only to check a Pro licence and, if you allow it, to see whether a new version is available.</p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
